 6. 💼 New this morning: Muse for small business 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg unveils Muse Charm during the Meta Connect event in Menlo Park, Calif., on Sept. 23. Photo: Carlos Barria/Reuters Meta announced Muse for Small Businesses this morning, expanding its consumer AI agent to a new market, Axios' Ina Fried writes. 

 Why it matters: Facebook's parent is moving into an area long dominated by companies such as Microsoft, bringing its viral consumer AI agent and broader AI infrastructure to businesses of all sizes. Zoom in: Meta is pitching Muse as a digital operations layer for small businesses that often lack the time or money to hire specialists for every function.

 For example, a business owner can ask Muse to analyze sales, campaigns and social activity and develop a growth plan. It can also help manage cash flow and inventory, draft customer communications and create ads and other content, including by analyzing what has worked previously. Share this story ... Read the announcement . 🦆 Power moves: Tucker Bounds, a Meta veteran (and proud Oregonian) who first went to work in Menlo Park in 2011, was elevated to Vice President, Global Communications and Public Affairs. 

 David Ginsberg, who held that role, is shifting to a new AI-focused innovation role as VP, Product, Insights Innovation. More from Sara Fischer . 
 
